/**
 * Overnight-Index Curve Bootstrap Config and Pillar Population Script
 *
 * Seeds one bootstrap config for the overnight-index curve of each currency the
 * synthetic Bloomberg feed quotes, other than USD, which
 * refdata_ir_curve_bootstrap_configs_populate.sql seeds. The FX volatility
 * surface reads the forward to each expiry from the published curves of the two
 * currencies of a pair, so the seven other currencies of the derived FX pairs
 * come first: EUR-ESTR, GBP-SONIA, JPY-TONA, CHF-SARON, AUD-AONIA, CAD-CORRA
 * and NZD-NZONIA. Twelve more follow: CLP-CAMARA, COP-IBR, CZK-CZEONIA,
 * DKK-DESTR, HKD-HONIA, INR-MIBOR, KRW-KOFR, MXN-TIIE, SEK-SWESTR, SGD-SORA,
 * TRY-TLREF and ZAR-ZARONIA. Each name is the id of the index's row in
 * ores_refdata_overnight_index_conventions_tbl.
 *
 * Eight currencies of the feed have no config here. BRL and NOK state day
 * counts, BUS/252 and ACT/ACT.ISMA, that the bootstrap engine does not
 * implement. CNY and TWD have no overnight index convention. CNH names HIBOR,
 * a term rate, and PLN names POLONIA, whose route is not read; neither is
 * bootstrapped. ILS names SHIR and HUF names HUFONIA after the ceased and
 * misnamed feeds were replaced, but no stored rate carries either yet.
 *
 * Each config follows the USD one: a FUNDING curve, which discounts off nothing,
 * interpolated LOG_LINEAR_DISCOUNT, with the tenor convention RATES_SPOT_FORWARD
 * and the split tenor 30Y. The day count is the overnight index's own, as its
 * convention row states it: ACT/360 (A360) or ACT/365 fixed (A365F).
 *
 * The seven pillars of each config ladder the terms the synthetic Bloomberg feed
 * publishes for the currency, as the USD config does: a 3M deposit from spot, a
 * 6M forward rate agreement from spot, then swaps from spot to 12M, 2Y, 5Y, 10Y
 * and 30Y. Every pillar names the currency's one ladder series, seeded by
 * marketdata_market_series_overnight_curves_populate.sql, and finds its own rung
 * by its end tenor. The config's output_series_id is that script's curve series.
 *
 * This script is idempotent - uses INSERT ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE.
 */

